@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}
<div class="text-center">
    <h1 class="display-4">Sports Application</h1>
</div>

<div class="d-flex justify-content-center mt-4">
    <a href="/Applications" class="btn btn-primary mx-2">Applications</a>
    @* <a href="/SelectApplication" class="btn btn-secondary mx-2">Select Application</a> *@
    <a class="btn btn-primary mx-2" asp-controller="SelectApplication" asp-action="Index">Select Application</a>

</div>

@* This code creates the home page for your web app.
What it does:
•	Sets the page title to "Home Page".
•	Displays a large heading: "Sports Application" in the center.
•	Shows two buttons in the center:
•	Applications: Takes the user to the applications page.
•	Select Application: Takes the user to the select application page using the SelectApplication controller's Index action.
In short:
This page welcomes users and gives them quick access to view applications or select an application type.
 *@